# Documentation claims

Claim vocabulary lives in `docs/README.md`. Do not invent a parallel scheme.

Two axes. Evidence strength is the ledger tag. Novelty — `KNOWN`, `REPARAMETERIZATION`, `PROJECT-SPECIFIC`, `OPEN` — is prose annotation and never a ledger tag.

Live publication work is the Juggler–Collatz programme (Papers A–E).
Earlier independent research is available through `docs/history.md`.

1. `docs/theory/juggler_finite_dynamics_note.md`
2. `docs/theory/juggler_parity_discrepancy_note.md`
3. `docs/juggler_branch_ledger.md`
4. `docs/theory/juggler_fate_almost_all_note.md`
5. `docs/theory/juggler_signed_collatz_note.md`
6. `docs/theory/theorem_ledger.md`

Collatz is one application: `docs/collatz_mathematics.md`. Use the seven ledger tags; do not write `PROVED`. Do not write “we solved Collatz” or “we solved Juggler”: if a matching `EXACT` statement exists, state the theorem, not the slogan.

`docs/theory/theorem_ledger.md` is generated. Edit the JSON, then render.

`docs/research_journal.md` holds at most twelve recent decisions; do not auto-open
Milestone *N+1*. A CLOSE / REFUTED entry links its canonical obstruction record.

New `REFUTED` ledger rows and CLOSE dossiers must be cited in a record under
`docs/negative_knowledge/` (`tests/integration/test_negative_knowledge.py`).
Run `python tools/research_memory.py` to refresh the generated directory;
do not edit `docs/negative_knowledge.md` by hand.

New problems copy `docs/problems/TEMPLATE.md`. Cite `literature/` ids.

Every `docs/problems/*.md` keeps all template headings, including `## Branch budget`, `## Decision`, and `## Publication assessment`. `tests/integration/test_problem_dossiers.py` enforces this. Method: `docs/methodology.md`.
